<title>SOUTH KOREA: LG Elec takes biggest stake in Kukdong.</title>
<headline>LG Elec takes biggest stake in Kukdong.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>LG Electronics Inc has bought a 23 percent stake in Kukdong City Gas Co to become the largest shareholder of the gas firm, a Kukdong statement said on Friday.</p>
<p>The purchase was made from four individuals.  </p>
<p>LG Electronics, flagship of the LG Group, bought 1.38 million shares of Kukdong, the statement said.</p>
<p>It did not give further details.</p>
<p>Earlier this month, two other units of the LG Group -- LG Cable and Machinery Ltd and LG-Caltex Oil Corp -- announced the purchase of a combined 28 percent stake in Kukdong from France's Esys Montenay SA.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
